# Purity

`src/core` has **no DOM, no I/O, no `Date`, no `Math.random`, no `console`.**
It imports only `src/core`.

Everything the engines need arrives in the `GameState` they were handed, or in
the bundle and manifest bound to them. Nothing is read from the world at play
time.

This is what makes the fight simulator possible. F2 and F6 (GRAMMAR.md) run ten
thousand fights per PR; that only works because a fight is a pure function of
state and seed. A single `Date.now()` in `src/core` costs the fairness proof.

> "load" means validate, not read from disk. A `src/core` function takes the
> already-parsed value; the caller does the reading.
